{
  "schema": "ora.toolkit-tool.v1",
  "name": "grasp_plan",
  "description": "Generate inspectable public RGB-D grasp candidates for one current target.\nUse when: current grounding or segmentation identifies the intended object and you need parallel-jaw poses.\nEffect: read-only; queries Contact-GraspNet using the selected source-camera RGB-D and compiles poses to the public TCP convention. Optional synchronized views provide review evidence.\nReturns: up to three candidates, complete world-frame pregrasp_pose and contact_pose, each with approach_world and jaw_line_world, the world directions of its approach axis and jaw line (move_pose's world_axes fields), copyable bounded contact_approach targets, predicted opening, compiler checks and labeled review images. Reachability is delegated to move_pose; this call does not run a motion probe or return a plan_ref. Inspect every candidate panel and choose target identity and geometry independently of rank. For this atomic surface, command the selected pregrasp_pose with move_pose, then read the receipt and fresh observation before approaching or closing with set_gripper. Re-plan candidates after any world action. Pose handoff: when manually commanding a returned world pose, set position_mode=absolute and orientation_mode=absolute_quaternion, then copy position_m and orientation_xyzw unchanged. Send these fields at the top level. Choose interaction by the intended physical contact. Schema example only; replace the illustrative pose with your selected current result:\n{\"tool\":\"move_pose\",\"arguments\":{\"position_mode\":\"absolute\",\"position_m\":[0.1,0.0,0.9],\"orientation_mode\":\"absolute_quaternion\",\"orientation_xyzw\":[0.0,0.0,0.0,1.0],\"interaction\":\"precision\"}}\nDoes not: plan trajectories, certify reachability, move the robot, command a gripper, use object ground truth, certify retention or report task success. Backend rank is not a success probability. Missing optional review cameras do not invalidate usable primary input.\nOn error: Refused: a target_ref unknown in this round (target_ref_unavailable) or bound to an earlier observation (stale_observation); max_candidates outside 1 to 3; unusable primary RGB-D or a transient backend failure (grasp_proposal_failed); a request the grasp-proposal service rejects (invalid_arguments, with the service's detail). Not refused but moved to diagnostics.rejected: a candidate whose predicted opening exceeds the 80 mm nominal ceiling, or whose controlled point or pregrasp lies outside the action workspace; with none left the result is status no_candidate. Obtain a better current view or select another target or candidate. Recompute after the target or observation changes. After a submitted motion fails, use its phase and measured residual to choose the next action. Retention evidence remains advisory. Candidate order: the grasp service's order, truncated to max_candidates; no inverse kinematics is checked before display on this backend.",
  "inputSchema": {
    "additionalProperties": false,
    "properties": {
      "max_candidates": {
        "default": 3,
        "description": "Maximum alternatives to inspect from this one query, from one through three, default 3: the front of the grasp service's order. This truncates a call-local ranking and does not select a grasp or request repeated planning. Null means omitted.",
        "maximum": 3,
        "minimum": 1,
        "type": [
          "integer",
          "null"
        ]
      },
      "target_ref": {
        "description": "Exactly one target_ref returned by vision_ground or vision_segment for the current immutable observation; do not copy an older reference after the world or observation changes.",
        "pattern": "^target-[0-9a-f]{24}$",
        "type": "string"
      }
    },
    "required": [
      "target_ref"
    ],
    "type": "object"
  },
